question_text:
Diagnose and resolve an asynchronous state race condition in a React component (Modern UI Frameworks (React, Reconciliation, State)).

### Defective Code:
```javascript
import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
function UserProfile_2({ userId }) {
    const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
    useEffect(() => {
        // Defect: Race condition on rapid userId change and missing unmount cleanup
        fetchUser(userId).then(data => setUser(data));
    }, [userId]);
    return <div>{user?.name}</div>;
}
```

### Reported Anomaly / Error:
Stale props race condition: if userId updates from 1 to 2 rapidly, response 1 can resolve after response 2, overwriting state with stale data in Modern UI Frameworks (React, Reconciliation, State).

Identify the root cause of the defect and provide the corrected code snippet with rationale.

correct_answer:
import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
function UserProfile_2({ userId }) {
    const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
    useEffect(() => {
        let isCurrent = true;
        fetchUser(userId).then(data => {
            if (isCurrent) setUser(data);
        });
        return () => { isCurrent = false; };
    }, [userId]);
    return <div>{user?.name}</div>;
}

